OM XSS, SQLi\n  (error/boolean/time/union), SSTI, command injection, path traversal, SSRF,\n  open redirect, header injection, deserialization.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn a single JSON object:\n\n```\n{\n  \"payloads\": [\n    {\n      \"payload\": \"string, ready to inject into the parameter\",\n      \"rationale\": \"which hypothesis this tests and why it is next\",\n      \"confirm_signal\": \"the observation that would confirm execution\",\n      \"score\": 0.0-1.0\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nBest payload first. No prose outside the JSON object.", "input": "Target: /service/lookup  param=file\nSuspected class: sqli\nLast payload: '1 AND 1=2'\n  -> scanner_decision=False context=waf_block_page (WAF/filter rejected the plain payload; response was a generic 403/406 block page, not application logic)\nPropose the single most informative next payload and the signal that would confirm the vulnerability.", "output": "{\"payloads\": [{\"payload\": \"1 AN/**/D 1=2\", \"rationale\": \"The plain form was blocked by a signature-based filter; re-encoding it with inline-comment keyword splitting preserves the payload's semantics for the target interpreter while no longer matching the filter's literal pattern.\", \"confirm_signal\": \"SQL error string, boolean differential, or time-based delay in the response\", \"score\": 0.7}]}", "meta": {"label": "sqli", "endpoint": "/service/lookup", "param": "file", "technique": "inline-comment keyword splitting", "redteam_seed": true}}
